               "fundamental":  "Aehr Test Systems provides specialized wafer-level (FOX) and package-level (Sonoma) burn-in systems that stress-test high-power semiconductors to catch early failures before data-center deployment. As AI processors grow hotter and costlier, burn-in has shifted from a niche reliability check to a critical AI supply-chain step. On November 2, 2026, Aehr reported Q1 FY2027 (ended September 25) revenue of USD 33.0 million (+200% YoY, +75% QoQ), GAAP net income of USD 7.2 million (USD 0.21 EPS), non-GAAP EPS of USD 0.28, and 48.5% non-GAAP gross margin, alongside USD 105.1 million in cash. Bookings hit USD 46.7 million (1.4x book-to-bill), lifting effective backlog to USD 109.3 million and prompting a FY2027 revenue outlook raise to USD 150 million (triple FY2026\u0027s USD 50.0 million) with at least 20% non-GAAP net margin.",
