               "opportunity":  "The divergence between AEHR\u0027s 67% stock pullback and its tripling revenue outlook creates a cleaner fundamental backdrop than August\u0027s euphoria. Effective backlog of USD 109.3 million already covers over 70% of the USD 150 million FY2027 revenue target, improving near-term visibility. Expanding Southeast Asia capacity (20+ Sonoma systems monthly), a second-generation hyperscaler AI chip win, a Taiwan OSAT FOX-XP wafer-level evaluation for calendar 2027, and a pipeline exceeding a dozen prospective AI, silicon photonics, and SiC customers offer multi-year diversification.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "The page\u0027s AI-opportunity profile understates Aehr\u0027s current AI revenue exposure and warrants an upward revision. With Q1 FY2027 revenue tripling year-over-year to USD 33.0 million and FY2027 guidance raised to USD 150 million primarily on hyperscale AI processor burn-in demand, AI is now the core growth engine rather than a secondary contributor. Market growth also merits a modest nudge higher as high-power AI chips adopt package- and wafer-level burn-in. However, keeping position and bottleneck-pricing power conservative remains appropriate given heavy reliance on one lead hyperscaler and potential test-equipment competition, while optionality looks fair.",
