               "summary":  "Coherent (NYSE:COHR) jumped 15.27% to $215.81 on Nov 23, 2026 after Nvidia reinstated CEO Jensen Huang, reversing a sharp sell-off tied to Nvidia\u0027s mid-November leadership turmoil. Underneath the volatility, fundamentals accelerated: Q1 FY2027 revenue (Nov 4) climbed 50% year-over-year to $2.37B, alongside a five-year, ~$20B PhotonLink optics contract and a $2.0B buyback authorized Nov 18. Still, heavy $776M quarterly capex pushed free cash flow negative, and shares remain 51% below their $440 high under all major moving averages—leaving the long-term moat intact but technicals bearish.",
