               "fundamental":  "Dell sits at the rack-integration layer of the AI value chain, assembling Nvidia and AMD silicon with networking, cooling, and storage for hyperscalers and enterprises. Its latest reported quarter, Q2 FY27 (September 1, 2026), delivered record revenue of $47.0 billion (+58% YoY) and non-GAAP EPS of $7.04 (+203% YoY). Infrastructure Solutions Group revenue surged 89% to $31.8 billion—including $16.4 billion from AI servers—while Client Solutions (PCs) rose 20% to $15.0 billion. Management lifted FY27 revenue guidance to $192.0 billion and AI server revenue to $74 billion, backed by a $95 billion backlog. Heading into Q3 FY27 earnings after market close on November 24 (consensus ~$49.3 billion revenue, ~$6.60 non-GAAP EPS), the key fundamental test is converting backlog into cash and defending margins as memory inflation squeezes fixed-price contracts.",
