               "opportunity":  "For long-term AI-infrastructure investors, DOCN offers tangible proof that a developer-focused cloud can capture production AI inference without losing its core identity. With AI Customer ARR already at $376M, 90% cross-usage into core cloud services, and $1M+ ARR customers up 273% YoY to $386M, the company is scaling upmarket while maintaining 45% Adjusted EBITDA margins and 20% trailing free-cash-flow margins. If management delivers on its 60%+ 2027 revenue growth outlook without heavy equity dilution, the 58% drawdown from $187.50 could reset valuation attractively once the chart stabilizes.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "The page\u0027s AI-opportunity profile looks too low on AI revenue exposure and should be moved meaningfully higher. With AI Customer ARR hitting $376M (+288% YoY) in Q3 2026—roughly a third of full-year revenue—and inference demand powering a 60%+ 2027 revenue outlook, AI is now DigitalOcean\u0027s main growth engine rather than a side bet. Market growth also merits a slight upward revision given surging agentic inference adoption. Conversely, keeping bottleneck and pricing power near the bottom remains accurate: DOCN buys Nvidia and AMD GPUs and must raise capital to compete with hyperscalers and neoclouds.",
