               "summary":  "DigitalOcean jumped 18.3% to $78.98 on Nov 23, 2026 in a broad AI-sector relief rally, yet remains 58% below its $187.50 52-week high. Fundamentals accelerated sharply in Q3 2026 (Nov 3), with revenue up 40% YoY to $321.2M, AI Customer ARR surging 288% to $376M, and management projecting 60%+ revenue growth in 2027. However, a concurrent $1.0B at-the-market share offering, softer Q4 EPS guidance ($0.30–$0.32) during data-center expansion, and analyst target cuts keep the chart in a bearish downtrend.",
               "technical":  "Despite jumping 18.3% to $78.98 on Nov 23, 2026 (opening at $80.01, peaking at $81.91, and closing below its open), DOCN remains in a bearish intermediate trend across its 500-day history. Price trades well below its exponential moving averages (EMAs, which track trend direction): EMA 50 at $99.94, EMA 200 at $104.78, and EMA 100 at $109.12. With EMA 50 beneath EMA 200, overhead resistance stacks heavily across $99.94–$109.12. Momentum shows only early stabilization. MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) stays deeply negative at -8.57, though edging above its -9.04 signal line turned the histogram marginally positive (+0.47). RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold, above 70 overbought) recovered to 42.38, still under the 50 neutral line. Within Bollinger Bands (a volatility envelope around the 20-day average), wide bands from $63.88 support to $105.29 reflect high volatility, with price rebounding toward middle-band resistance at $84.59 while sitting in the bottom third of its $42.01–$187.50 52-week range. Crucially, Nov 23 volume (3.74M shares) trailed the 20-day average (4.13M), signaling a relief bounce rather than confirmed institutional accumulation."
