               "summary":  "Alphabet (GOOGL) closed at $282.10 on November 23, 2026—up 6.34% in a broad AI relief rally, yet still 31% below its $408.61 52-week high. Shares plunged roughly 12.6% after October 28 Q3 results revealed $51.4B in quarterly capital spending and -$9.1B in free cash flow, alongside a C$6B bond sale priced November 19. Operationally, Google Cloud surged 103% year-over-year to $30.7B with a $561B backlog, while new TPU 8tx/8i Max chips and Gemini 4 reinforced the long-term platform moat. Technically, the trend stays bearish pending a reclaim of key moving averages.",
               "technical":  "GOOGL\u0027s technical posture remains bearish despite its 6.34% bounce to $282.10 on November 23, 2026. Price sits well below all three exponential moving averages (EMAs—smoothed trend lines weighted toward recent prices): EMA 50 at $311.57, EMA 200 at $322.90, and EMA 100 at $325.11. With price trailing EMA 50 and EMA 50 sitting beneath EMA 200, the intermediate trend points firmly downward. Momentum is trying to stabilize but lacks confirmation: MACD (a 12/26/9 trend-momentum gauge) stays deeply negative at -12.74, though just above its -13.00 signal line for a slight +0.25 positive histogram, while RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) recovered only to a weak 41.04. Within the Bollinger Bands (20-day volatility channels around a $287.71 midpoint), GOOGL trades in the lower half between $260.18 lower-band support and $287.71 immediate resistance, just 6.8% above its $264.22 52-week low and 31% under its $408.61 high. Crucially, November 23 volume of 44.26M trailed the 20-day average of 46.30M and closed below the $284.28 open, signaling a sector-led relief rally rather than confirmed accumulation. Nearby support stands at $260–$264, with layered resistance at $287.71 and $311.57–$315.25."
