               "opportunity":  "With shares still 22.2% below their $1,714.09 52-week high despite record Q3 results and $1.35 billion midpoint Q4 revenue guidance, non-fundamental volatility has opened a gap between business momentum and price. Long-term AI infrastructure holders can track three structural catalysts: annualized capacity scaling from over $6 billion toward $8 billion by 2H 2027, rising module content across multiple cloud hyperscalers, and early sampling of 800-volt and gallium nitride (GaN) data-center power solutions for late 2027–2028, complemented by ramping 48V automotive power orders.",
