               "summary":  "Monolithic Power Systems (MPWR) jumped 16.8% to $1,333.88 on November 23, 2026 after Nvidia reinstated CEO Jensen Huang, reversing a sharp mid-November tech sell-off. Fundamentally, MPWR\u0027s October 29 Q3 2026 report confirmed surging AI demand: revenue crossed $1 billion for the first time at $1,202.4 million (+63.1% YoY), led by Enterprise Data up 164.6% YoY to $506.7 million, with Q4 guided to $1,315–$1,385 million. While the long-term moat remains intact, high volatility, unstacked moving averages, and a November 9 patent-trial loss keep the near-term technical picture neutral.",
               "technical":  "As of November 23, 2026, MPWR closed at $1,333.88 (+16.8% on the day), rebounding sharply above its three exponential moving averages (EMA — trend lines weighting recent prices): EMA 50 ($1,296.16), EMA 100 ($1,306.86), and EMA 200 ($1,266.19). While trading above EMA 200 preserves the longer-term uptrend, EMA 50 still sits below EMA 100, signaling an incomplete medium-term recovery. Momentum remains mixed: MACD (a trend-momentum gauge comparing fast and slow averages) is positive at 4.72 but trails its 10.15 signal line, leaving a negative -5.43 histogram. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold, over 70 overbought) sits neutrally at 52.32. Volatility is wide across the Bollinger Bands (a 20-day volatility channel) from $1,100.39 to $1,476.12, with price just above the $1,288.26 midline and at 56.8% of its $833.18–$1,714.09 52-week range (22.2% below the peak). Volume of 1.40 million shares beat the 1.19 million 20-day average by 17%, offering moderate confirmation. Near-term support clusters at $1,288–$1,307 and $1,266.19; resistance sits near $1,476.12 and $1,714.09."
