               "summary":  "Marvell Technology (MRVL) surged 18.37% to $144.74 on Nov 23, 2026 in a sector-wide rebound after Nvidia reinstated CEO Jensen Huang, yet shares remain 56% below their $329.88 52-week high. The sell-off followed Marvell\u0027s Nov 2 announcement of a $115 billion all-stock acquisition of optical supplier Lumentum, triggering equity-dilution fears, downgrades from TD Cowen and Bank of America, and antitrust concerns. Core AI demand remains robust—Q2 FY27 data center revenue jumped 46% YoY to $2.172 billion and Q3 guidance tracks $3.15 billion—keeping the long-term thesis on watch ahead of Dec 1 earnings.",
