               "summary":  "onsemi\u0027s November 23 rally of 9.75% to $66.77 looks like a relief bounce inside a broader downtrend, leaving the stock 50.5% below its $134.92 52-week high. Fundamentally, Q3 2026 results on November 2 showed strong execution: revenue rose 11% year-over-year to $1.722 billion, non-GAAP gross margin expanded to 41.2%, and AI data center sales surged 175% to $180 million alongside a $600 million Ferric deal. However, canceling its $2 billion Czech SiC expansion on November 6, soft Q4 auto guidance, and debt-funded Synaptics integration keep the moat thesis on watch.",
               "technical":  "Despite jumping 9.75% to $66.77 on November 23, ON\u0027s overall chart remains bearish. Price sits well below its exponential moving averages (EMAs — trend lines tracking average price over 50, 100, and 200 days), which are stacked in bearish order: EMA 50 ($72.87) under EMA 100 ($76.93) and EMA 200 ($77.04). Momentum confirms caution. The MACD (a trend-momentum oscillator) stands at -2.38, below its -1.96 signal line with a negative -0.42 histogram, while RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) reads 44.94—recovering toward neutral but still below the 50 midpoint. On volatility, shares rebounded sharply off the lower Bollinger Band ($60.83; a volatility envelope around the 20-day average) after closing at $60.84 on November 20, yet still sit in the lower quarter of their $44.56–$134.92 52-week range. Volume reached 14.65 million shares, 27% above the 11.54 million 20-day average, showing genuine dip-buying. Near-term resistance sits at the $69.74 middle band and $72.87 EMA 50, with key support at $60.83."
