               "opportunityCheck":  "The page\u0027s AI-opportunity profile largely holds up, but the bottleneck and pricing power rating looks materially too low. While Palantir sells software rather than scarce chips, Q3 2026 delivered 62% adjusted operating margins, 165% net dollar retention, and $146 million average trailing revenue across its top 20 accounts—proof of strong pricing power. Even UK ministers criticizing the firm extended its NHS platform two years because replacing it takes years. Moving bottleneck and pricing power meaningfully higher, and nudging market position slightly up, better fits reality, while sluggish international commercial growth (+21% YoY) keeps overseas optionality grounded.",
