               "summary":  "Palantir (PLTR) jumped 11.06% to $159.36 on Nov 23, 2026, rebounding from an AI-sector sell-off after Sovereign AI partner Nvidia reinstated CEO Jensen Huang. Operationally, Q3 2026 results on Nov 2 beat expectations: revenue rose 96% YoY to $2.313 billion, U.S. commercial jumped 148% to $984 million, and FY 2026 revenue guidance rose to $8.530–$8.534 billion. Still, PLTR sits 25.2% off its $212.94 high and below key moving averages amid high-multiple compression, slower 6% YoY bookings growth, and the UK\u0027s Nov 16 plan to end its NHS contract in 2029.",
               "technical":  "PLTR\u0027s technical posture remains bearish despite Nov 23\u0027s sharp +11.06% rebound to $159.36 (intraday range $154.57–$161.19). Price trades below all three Exponential Moving Averages (EMA — weighted trend averages): EMA 50 ($174.55), EMA 100 ($170.06), and EMA 200 ($161.68). Because EMA 50 still sits above EMA 100 and EMA 200, the multi-month uptrend has avoided a bearish crossover, yet Monday\u0027s rally stalled just shy of immediate resistance at EMA 200 ($161.68). Momentum confirms caution: MACD (12/26/9 — a trend-momentum gauge) stands at -9.13 below its -7.55 signal line, leaving a negative -1.58 histogram, while RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum index; below 30 is oversold) recovered only to a weak-neutral 41.71. On Bollinger Bands (20/2 — a volatility channel), price sits in the lower half between the $140.16 lower band and $169.85 middle band, roughly at the midpoint of its $106.37–$212.94 52-week range (25.2% below the peak). Encouragingly, Nov 23 volume hit 32.01 million shares—24.3% above the 25.75 million 20-day average—indicating genuine dip-buying near the $140–$145 support zone, though reclaiming $161.68 and $170 resistance is needed to repair the chart."
